  "mathematics": [
    "The original implicit finite-volume equation, boundary conditions, corrected nonorthogonal flux, material conservative volume versus native FV volume, caloric integral and nonlinear stopping tolerances are retained.",
    "The shared FP64 solver uses diagonal-preconditioned CG instead of native DIC-PCG. This changes linear iteration counts and rounding, but not the equation or requested residual tolerances. Independent native matrix, true residual and heat-flux oracles bound the resulting error.",
    "Local scalar cyclic boundaries are assembled in CSR. Processor and other coupled interfaces retain native communication, with CUDA local arithmetic. Empty MPI partitions are supported.",
    "The local CG recurrence and every stopping decision execute inside a conditional CUDA graph. Thirty scaled matrix comparisons plus min/max-iteration and relative-tolerance cases match an unbatched execution of the same recurrence bitwise.",
    "Material conduction uses the accepted GPU inventory. Endpoint energy and EOS publish only after all cells succeed, preserving the existing candidate transaction semantics.",
    "Table properties, exact piecewise caloric integrals, material polynomial/NASA7 secants and Aitken history retain their original formulas. Ordered Aitken and host conservation reductions preserve their established summation order."
  ],
  "remaining_host_work": [
    "OpenFOAM field and matrix mirrors, selected boundary policy calls, mesh geometry and MPI communication still execute on the host.",
    "Ordered diagnostic conservation reductions remain on the host. Some interface property consumers outside the nonlinear conduction owner still use their original CPU helpers.",
    "Radiation and geometry migration are separate subsequent layers; this is not a claim of a completely resident five-layer application."
  ],
